# OceanScale Cursor Rules

Read before any work:

- `AGENTS.md` — cross-tool agent instructions
- `POSITIONING.md` — brand / scope / voice / lexicon / banned words
- `DESIGN.md` — visual brand law
- `ARCHITECTURE.md` — technical architecture
- `GLOSSARY.md` — terminology

## Copy contributions

POSITIONING.md governs all user-facing copy.
- §3 anchor sentence is quoted verbatim, not paraphrased.
- §5 enemy line is quoted verbatim.
- §7 lexicon — use canonical spellings.
- §8 banned words — enforced. Do not commit copy that violates.

Bilingual zh/en is mandatory. EN and ZH are both canonical, neither is a translation.

## Visual contributions

DESIGN.md governs all visuals.
- §2 banned patterns — enforced.
- §3 required patterns — preferred.
- §8 wordmark — OceanScale is one word, two caps.

## Code style

- Python: 3.12+, type hints on public APIs, `ruff format`, no needless comments.
- TypeScript / Astro: strict mode.
- Conventional Commits.
- One logical change per commit.
- Tests after every change.

## Monorepo

Sub-packages may have their own `AGENTS.md`. Read it before working in that directory:
- `oceanscale/AGENTS.md` — Python package
- `website/AGENTS.md` — Astro app
- `benchmarks/AGENTS.md` — perf tests
- `notebooks/AGENTS.md` — Colab notebooks
